{"id": "edge_874", "source": "annales", "target": "quebec_historiography", "relationship": "Labroussian economic and social history at Laval", "type": "connection", "relationship_kind": "contribution", "directed": true, "source_ids": ["qcreq_savard_1974", "qcreq_ouellet_1966", "qcreq_charron_dechene", "qcreq_dechene_1974", "qcreq_linteau_1983"], "evidence_note": "Savard (1974) says Ouellet owed a debt to Labrousse and Chaunu; Robert Mandrou prefaced Ouellet’s 1966 book (review heading). Dechêne trained in France in the Annales milieu of Mandrou and Goubert before her Paris doctorate (1973), published as Habitants et marchands (1974) (Charron, Dictionnaire universel des créatrices; formal supervision not asserted). Linteau (1983) says social history began in Quebec in the 1960s under Annales influence but that his generation was shaped more by French and Quebec sociologists and American historians. Specific contributions to the Laval and New France strands, not an Annales origin for Quebec historiography.", "classification_basis": "editorial_review", "map_label": "Annales resources: Labrousse, Mandrou", "proposal_id": "qcreq_rel_01"}
